PN,31207
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786403882
OL,3,CMet Office considers rare extreme heat
OL,4,Cwarning as it forecasts 36C highs
OL,6,FSo far, the extreme weather of summer
OL,7,F2026 has included two record-breaking
OL,8,Fheatwaves in May and June that led to
OL,9,Fmore than 2,800 excess deaths.
OL,11,FSubscribe for free to our weekly
OL,12,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,13,Fcoverage from ITV News. Direct to your
OL,14,Finbox every Friday morning.
OL,16,FTwo more heatwaves in July, the driest
OL,17,FJuly in England and Wales since
OL,18,Frecords began in 1836, have fuelled
OL,19,Fdrought and wildfires.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/8
